"""Build the complete reviewed METABRIC gene-set catalogue after thesis steps01–04.

Inputs are the gene annotation and summary written by03, and the gene-only
universe, definitions and completion metadata written by04. Clinical tables,
patient expression values, patient scores and outcome labels are not read.

All reviewed group definitions are included at the end of this file as plain
TSV data: group names, source references, versions, restrictions and complete
reviewed Entrez memberships. No historical archive, private directory layout,
local Python package or network download is required.

This step consolidates reviewed gene definitions. It does not repeat the
original literature extraction or identifier adjudication. It preserves the
accepted gene sets, signed arms, unresolved identities and deferred candidates.
It keeps earlier incomplete signatures as documentary references. Membership
in the catalogue never authorizes a new score, predictor or outcome analysis.

Normal execution, after completing01–04 within the same project:
    python 05_build_metabric_gene_set_catalogue.py

The project root is the nearest enclosing Git or Python project, or the folder
containing this script when neither marker exists. Previous outputs are located
by their file structure, regardless of directory names. Discovery is limited to
six directory levels within that project and skips environments and caches.
Exactly one candidate for each previous step must be found; ambiguous candidates
are never selected by modification time. Explicit path options remain available.

Results are written to modeling_data/gene_set_catalogue_v1 under the project
root. If that path already exists, a new dated directory is selected. Previous
results are never overwritten. The selected paths are printed before execution.

Use the Python environment used for04 (Python3.10 or newer). This file itself
uses only the Python standard library. --self-test reads no external inputs.
--export-zip optionally creates one verified ZIP containing the generated files.

Source group definitions retain their original source references and terms.
MSigDB material is attributed to Broad Institute, MIT and the Regents of the
University of California under CC BY4.0, with collection-specific terms retained.
See https://www.gsea-msigdb.org/gsea/msigdb_license_terms.jsp
"""

